# Patent Claims

**Claim 1.** A system for reconstructing joint biophysical properties from multiple imaging modalities, the system comprising:

a data acquisition module configured to receive a plurality of imaging datasets corresponding to a common anatomical region of interest, wherein each imaging dataset is obtained from a distinct imaging modality selected from the group consisting of magnetic resonance imaging, computed tomography, ultrasound imaging, positron emission tomography, optical coherence tomography, and elastography;

a preprocessing module configured to spatially co-register the plurality of imaging datasets to a common reference coordinate system, thereby generating a set of co-registered imaging datasets;

a joint reconstruction module configured to generate an initial estimate of a plurality of biophysical parameters associated with the anatomical region of interest based on the set of co-registered imaging datasets, wherein the plurality of biophysical parameters comprises at least two of tissue stiffness, tissue density, water content, perfusion rate, and metabolic activity;

a forward modeling module configured to compute a plurality of simulated imaging signals corresponding to each of the distinct imaging modalities based on the initial estimate of the plurality of biophysical parameters;

a comparison module configured to calculate a difference metric between the plurality of simulated imaging signals and the plurality of co-registered imaging datasets;

a threshold evaluation module configured to compare the difference metric to a predetermined difference threshold; and

an iterative refinement module configured to, in response to the difference metric exceeding the predetermined difference threshold, adjust the plurality of biophysical parameters and provide the adjusted plurality of biophysical parameters to the forward modeling module for recomputation of the plurality of simulated imaging signals,

wherein the iterative refinement module is further configured to output a final estimate of the plurality of biophysical parameters in response to the difference metric falling below the predetermined difference threshold.

**Claim 2.** The system of claim 1, wherein the joint reconstruction module is configured to enforce a shared anatomical structure constraint across the plurality of biophysical parameters derived from the distinct imaging modalities.

**Claim 3.** The system of claim 1, wherein the forward modeling module comprises a plurality of modality-specific physics-based simulation engines, each configured to generate a simulated imaging signal for a corresponding imaging modality based on a shared set of the plurality of biophysical parameters.

**Claim 4.** The system of claim 1, wherein the difference metric comprises a weighted combination of a plurality of per-modality difference values, each per-modality difference value calculated between a respective simulated imaging signal and a corresponding co-registered imaging dataset.

**Claim 5.** The system of claim 4, wherein the weighted combination applies a weighting coefficient to each per-modality difference value based on a signal-to-noise ratio associated with the corresponding imaging modality.

**Claim 6.** The system of claim 1, wherein the iterative refinement module is configured to adjust the plurality of biophysical parameters using a gradient-based optimization algorithm that minimizes the difference metric.

**Claim 7.** The system of claim 6, wherein the gradient-based optimization algorithm comprises a regularization term that penalizes non-physical values of the plurality of biophysical parameters.

**Claim 8.** The system of claim 1, wherein the predetermined difference threshold is dynamically adjusted based on a number of iterations performed by the iterative refinement module.

**Claim 9.** The system of claim 1, further comprising a convergence monitoring module configured to terminate the iterative refinement module after a predetermined maximum number of iterations regardless of whether the difference metric falls below the predetermined difference threshold.

**Claim 10.** The system of claim 1, wherein the plurality of biophysical parameters is represented as a spatial map corresponding to a plurality of voxels within the anatomical region of interest.

**Claim 11.** The system of claim 1, wherein the joint reconstruction module comprises a machine learning model trained to generate the initial estimate of the plurality of biophysical parameters from the set of co-registered imaging datasets.

**Claim 12.** The system of claim 11, wherein the machine learning model comprises a convolutional neural network trained on a plurality of paired multimodal imaging datasets and corresponding known biophysical parameter values.

**Claim 13.** A method for reconstructing joint biophysical properties from multiple imaging modalities, the method comprising:

receiving a plurality of imaging datasets corresponding to a common anatomical region of interest, each imaging dataset obtained from a distinct imaging modality;

spatially co-registering the plurality of imaging datasets to a common reference coordinate system;

generating an initial estimate of a plurality of biophysical parameters based on the co-registered imaging datasets;

computing a plurality of simulated imaging signals corresponding to each of the distinct imaging modalities based on the initial estimate of the plurality of biophysical parameters;

calculating a difference metric between the plurality of simulated imaging signals and the co-registered imaging datasets;

comparing the difference metric to a predetermined difference threshold;

iteratively adjusting the plurality of biophysical parameters and recomputing the plurality of simulated imaging signals until the difference metric falls below the predetermined difference threshold; and

outputting a final estimate of the plurality of biophysical parameters upon determining that the difference metric falls below the predetermined difference threshold.

**Claim 14.** The method of claim 13, further comprising generating a confidence map indicating a spatial reliability of the final estimate of the plurality of biophysical parameters based on a rate of convergence of the difference metric during the iteratively adjusting step.

**Claim 15.** The method of claim 13, wherein iteratively adjusting the plurality of biophysical parameters comprises applying a Bayesian update based on a prior probability distribution associated with the plurality of biophysical parameters.

**Claim 16.** A non-transitory computer-readable medium storing instructions that, when executed by one or more processors, cause the one or more processors to perform operations comprising:

receiving a plurality of co-registered imaging datasets corresponding to a common anatomical region of interest, wherein each of the plurality of co-registered imaging datasets is derived from a distinct imaging modality;

jointly estimating a plurality of biophysical parameters based on the plurality of co-registered imaging datasets;

simulating, using a forward model, a plurality of imaging signals corresponding to the distinct imaging modalities based on the jointly estimated plurality of biophysical parameters;

determining a difference metric between the plurality of simulated imaging signals and the plurality of co-registered imaging datasets;

responsive to the difference metric exceeding a difference threshold, updating the plurality of biophysical parameters and repeating the simulating and determining operations; and

responsive to the difference metric being less than or equal to the difference threshold, storing the plurality of biophysical parameters as a final output.

**Claim 17.** The non-transitory computer-readable medium of claim 16, wherein the operations further comprise generating a visualization representing at least one of the plurality of biophysical parameters overlaid on at least one of the plurality of co-registered imaging datasets.

**Claim 18.** The non-transitory computer-readable medium of claim 16, wherein the distinct imaging modalities comprise at least a first modality sensitive to mechanical tissue properties and a second modality sensitive to functional tissue properties, and wherein the plurality of biophysical parameters jointly characterizes both mechanical and functional properties of the anatomical region of interest.
